{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792308701,"nonce":"QU9rD786gMegpBNfr1ZRaz8J3nQ=","title":"Resizable cannot be flattened with tokens","message":"Reported by the RayDE session building a VS Code-style workbench on ashui 3d9c201. Repro: RayDE at be30e7b, src/rayde/ui/{Workbench.hx,FileTabs.hx,rayde.css}; scripts/snapshot.sh writes pictures to bin/snapshots.\n\n**What happens**\n\n`.ui-resizable` always draws a border, a radius and the surface background, and `.ui-resizable-line` is always visible. A layout of separate cards with gaps needs `#id .ui-resizable {border-width:0; background:transparent}`, and then the hover, drag and focus colours have to be restated, because the id-qualified override out-specifies ashui's own rules.\n\n**What is wanted**\n\nTokens: `--ui-resizable-border`, `--ui-resizable-radius`, and the idle and hover line colours; or a bare prop.","files":null}]}